      "name": "The 5-minute test: find out why your brand isn't showing up on Google",
      "totalTime": "PT5M",
      "step": [
        { "@type": "HowToStep", "name": "Check your indexing", "text": "Type site:yourbrand.com into Google. The number of results ≈ what Google knows about your site. Compare it with your real page count: a massive gap = an indexing problem." },
        { "@type": "HowToStep", "name": "Check your branded queries", "text": "Search \"your brand + your hero product\". If your site isn't first, note who is: that's your hottest leak." },
        { "@type": "HowToStep", "name": "Search like a customer", "text": "Search for your hero product by what it does (\"curl cream for 4C hair\"), not by its range name. If you're nowhere within two pages, the naming problem is confirmed." },
        { "@type": "HowToStep", "name": "Open Search Console", "text": "In the Pages tab, the number of \"not indexed\" pages tells you the size of the job." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need to rebuild my site?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Almost never. In the vast majority of cases the existing structure can be fixed: indexing, naming, internal linking between pages. A rebuild is a last resort — and a poorly scoped rebuild is precisely one of the top causes of lost visibility." } },
